Martin Read wrote:

>For reference, Nethack *doesn't fit* into 640K of memory. Even Nethack
>3.1.3 didn't fit into 640K; there is much crawling-horror in the
>real-mode build rules for Nethack.

The last NetHack that fit into 640K without heroic measures was 2.3e.
3.0.X sprouted a bunch of optional features, apparently to get a stripped-
down game that could fit.  The wiki has the whole sad story at
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/MS-DOS .  The crawling horror started with
3.0.6, and we got a proper 32-bit version only with 3.1.0.

I have succeeded in building 3.4.3 to fit in 640K, but it's probably not
worthwhile anymore, because you practically need a 386 anyway to have
enough of that 640K free.  See
http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/e14f24e6d473577e/28508d92ac1e823a?lnk=st&q=&rnum=1



